-- ITEM #11: the stacks are NOT cached in locals here any more.
--
-- This file used to hold `local undoStack = BuildHistory.undoStack` and the
-- same for redo. BuildHistory.pushUndo then did `BuildHistory.redoStack = {}`,
-- replacing the table rather than emptying it -- so from the first undo onward
-- the local and the module field were two different tables, and any read
-- through the local saw a stack frozen in the past. BuildHistory now clears in
-- place and everything here goes through its API, so there is no second
-- reference left to fall out of step.

